1
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:20,640
Go... go left, left! Yes, yes, yes!

2
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:21,679
Go... go left, go left!

3
00:00:23,039 --> 00:00:24,000
I can't believe I got that kill!

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,920
Nice, nice, nice!

5
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:25,960
You're a pro! Ah, I'm dead, I'm dead!

6
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:26,399
Pro!

7
00:00:30,559 --> 00:00:31,399
What a pro! Pro, pro!

8
00:00:31,399 --> 00:00:32,799
Then you watch his back, he watches yours.

9
00:00:32,799 --> 00:00:33,520
Otherwise, on your own...

10
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:34,880
you definitely can't cover it all, right?

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,240
Anyway, it's really not hard. Not hard at all.

12
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:37,880
Lin Ran.

13
00:00:38,039 --> 00:00:38,439
There are some...

14
00:00:38,719 --> 00:00:39,799
And another thing is...

15
00:00:39,799 --> 00:00:40,600
Lin Ran, um...

16
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:41,840
between two people...

17
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:42,399
Lin Ran!

18
00:00:44,439 --> 00:00:45,240
Come home with me.

19
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:50,719
Attention, please.

20
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:53,920
The user at terminal 18 has logged off.

21
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:56,320
Please clean up the desk promptly.

22
00:01:02,079 --> 00:01:03,240
Look at the state of you.

23
00:01:03,679 --> 00:01:04,159
Let's go.

24
00:01:15,959 --> 00:01:16,719
A date?

25
00:01:17,599 --> 00:01:19,120
Yeah, don't you want to?

26
00:01:19,879 --> 00:01:20,920
Of course I want to.

27
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:22,879
It's just...

28
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,480
I haven't thought it through.

29
00:01:27,439 --> 00:01:28,560
Then think about it some more.

30
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:32,319
Where are you going?

31
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:33,480
To the bathroom.

32
00:01:42,319 --> 00:01:43,079
Alright.

33
00:01:43,719 --> 00:01:44,159
What are you all doing?

34
00:01:44,159 --> 00:01:46,000
Are you crazy?

35
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,079
Yeah, how can we make decisions for her?

36
00:01:48,519 --> 00:01:49,359
Why can't we?

37
00:01:49,959 --> 00:01:51,319
We're the same person anyway.

38
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,480
Have you forgotten a lesson from the past?

39
00:01:53,719 --> 00:01:54,920
What lesson from the past?

40
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:56,519
Fine, playing dumb, huh?

41
00:02:00,719 --> 00:02:01,879
Isn't this pretty cool?

42
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:04,319
Okay, when you went shopping yesterday,

43
00:02:04,319 --> 00:02:05,560
weren't you looking at that dress?

44
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,359
That's right, it looks pretty good.

45
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:08,400
It does look pretty good.

46
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,199
I'll buy it for you, it's fine.

47
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,080
We're easygoing.

48
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,159
The two of us don't mind.

49
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,599
But Lin Ran, because of this,

50
00:02:22,599 --> 00:02:23,680
cried her eyes out.

51
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,639
Yeah, a tattoo can still be removed.

52
00:02:25,759 --> 00:02:27,400
But choosing the wrong partner is serious.

53
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,680
Are you guys overthinking this?

54
00:02:29,879 --> 00:02:32,039
I wasn't really deciding for Lin Ran.

55
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,039
I just wanted to

56
00:02:34,599 --> 00:02:35,680
check him out for her.

57
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,439
You better take responsibility.

58
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,400
Alright.

59
00:02:38,479 --> 00:02:39,560
Stop nagging.

60
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:40,759
If anything goes wrong, it's on me.

61
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,400
Don't follow me.

62
00:02:51,479 --> 00:02:53,120
What took you so long?

63
00:02:53,599 --> 00:02:54,840
I told you I went to the bathroom.

64
00:02:58,159 --> 00:02:59,120
So,

65
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,719
were you serious about going on a date?

66
00:03:03,199 --> 00:03:04,000
Of course.

67
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:06,599
Great.

68
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,439
Where do you want to go?

69
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,400
Uncle! Uncle!

70
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,439
Where are you going?

71
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:13,240
I want to go too.

72
00:03:15,159 --> 00:03:15,719
Stop fooling around.

73
00:03:16,039 --> 00:03:17,159
I just want to cause trouble!

74
00:03:17,159 --> 00:03:17,840
I want to go!

75
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:18,759
I want to go!

76
00:03:19,599 --> 00:03:20,599
Why don't you bring her along?

77
00:03:20,599 --> 00:03:21,439
No, no, no need.

78
00:03:21,599 --> 00:03:23,080
I'll take Xiaomei back first.

79
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,400
Unless you buy me another ice cream.

80
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,000
Okay.

81
00:03:28,759 --> 00:03:30,960
Alright, I'll send you an address later.

82
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:31,960
We can meet up there.

83
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:32,960
Okay.

84
00:03:38,719 --> 00:03:39,400
Thanks.

85
00:03:40,319 --> 00:03:40,759
Bye-bye.

86
00:03:40,759 --> 00:03:41,560
See you in a bit.

87
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:59,639
So this is the date spot you mentioned.

88
00:04:00,199 --> 00:04:01,759
What, you don't like it?

89
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,599
N-No, it's not that.

90
00:04:04,039 --> 00:04:05,240
I'm just a bit surprised.

91
00:04:08,159 --> 00:04:08,960
Aren't we going?

92
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,000
What's on your mind?

93
00:04:29,279 --> 00:04:30,360
Nothing.

94
00:04:31,399 --> 00:04:32,439
Nothing.

95
00:04:35,959 --> 00:04:36,600
Let's go.

96
00:04:44,959 --> 00:04:45,879
Are you happy?

97
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:51,240
I am.

98
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:01,079
I knew you'd come.

99
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:01,920
By the way,

100
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,560
this is the substitute I told you about.

101
00:05:03,839 --> 00:05:04,360
David.

102
00:05:07,959 --> 00:05:09,199
Let's skip the small talk.

103
00:05:09,399 --> 00:05:10,600
I have a flight to catch.

104
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:11,879
Let's get right to it.

105
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
David, this game is one or the other.

106
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:32,240
I'm rooting for you.

107
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,399
Okay.

108
00:05:56,959 --> 00:05:57,759
Lin.

109
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:00,600
What are you guys doing?

110
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:01,800
Playing a game.

111
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,399
You play video games?

112
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,759
There's a lot I can do.

113
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,959
So you're playing against him?

114
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:16,959
Come on, come on!

115
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,399
All right, let's get started then.

116
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,160
You got this!

117
00:06:25,399 --> 00:06:26,279
Don't embarrass yourself.

118
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,279
Show them what you've got.

119
00:06:40,879 --> 00:06:41,680
Stop hissing.

120
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,279
It's just a draw.

121
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,439
Yeah, you'll definitely win.

122
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:49,360
I wouldn't be so sure.

123
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,240
If you lose,

124
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:53,120
don't ever brag about

125
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,240
how good you are at gaming.

126
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:56,319
That's never gonna happen.

127
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:20,800
Champion

128
00:07:21,279 --> 00:07:22,399
Champion, come here.

129
00:07:24,519 --> 00:07:25,759
Champion. Champion.

130
00:07:25,759 --> 00:07:28,000
Congrats on qualifying for the team.

131
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,040
Thank you.

132
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:33,000
But... I can't join your team anymore.

133
00:07:38,199 --> 00:07:39,000
Why?

134
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:40,439
Because I feel like...

135
00:07:40,439 --> 00:07:42,199
this goes against why I started gaming.

136
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:43,920
The reason I like gaming

137
00:07:44,199 --> 00:07:45,279
is that I don't want to be tied down.

138
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:48,399
But once a hobby becomes a career,

139
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:49,800
it's just not the same anymore.

140
00:07:53,879 --> 00:07:54,639
Okay.

141
00:07:55,279 --> 00:07:56,279
Then I respect your decision.

142
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,879
Anyway, if you figure things out later,

143
00:07:58,879 --> 00:07:59,800
or change your mind,

144
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:00,680
come find me anytime.

145
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:01,439
I'm off.

146
00:08:02,199 --> 00:08:02,800
See ya.

147
00:08:22,199 --> 00:08:24,000
What? You want to talk me out of it too?

148
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,199
Not at all.

149
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,399
I think you make perfect sense.

150
00:08:28,959 --> 00:08:30,000
Then why are you looking at me?

151
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,559
Can I play a couple rounds with you?

152
00:08:38,679 --> 00:08:40,200
Bring it on. Who's afraid?

153
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:46,240
Don't go easy on me.

154
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:52,559
Wait a sec.

155
00:08:52,559 --> 00:08:54,080
Here. No, no, no! Don't move, don't move!

156
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,000
Take this! I'm not waiting!

157
00:08:55,519 --> 00:08:56,799
I... I haven't used my ultimate yet!

158
00:08:56,799 --> 00:08:58,120
Hit, hit, hit!

159
00:08:58,559 --> 00:08:59,919
Take this! No waiting, no waiting!

160
00:08:59,919 --> 00:09:00,639
Uppercut!

161
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:02,879
My bad. Why can't I use my ultimate?

162
00:09:02,919 --> 00:09:03,759
Wait, wait! I used it!

163
00:09:03,759 --> 00:09:04,320
I used it!

164
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:05,039
Wait, wait!

165
00:09:05,039 --> 00:09:06,120
Fire!

166
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:08,679
Wow...

167
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:10,600
I can't beat you at all.

168
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,559
It'd be a miracle if you could.

169
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,000
One more round.

170
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,320
You're on.

171
00:09:18,159 --> 00:09:19,279
Let's switch characters.

172
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,399
My time is up.

173
00:09:28,679 --> 00:09:29,600
What do you mean?

174
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,159
The rest of the time is yours.

175
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,039
You really are strict about this.

176
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:38,000
Why? Don't you need the time?

177
00:09:40,159 --> 00:09:41,240
Well...

178
00:09:41,759 --> 00:09:42,799
It's not that I don't need it.

179
00:09:57,519 --> 00:09:58,200
What's wrong?

180
00:10:00,399 --> 00:10:02,080
Let's go to the next date spot.

181
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:05,639
Sure.

182
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:23,240
Is this your hobby too?

183
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,600
Why, is it not allowed?

184
00:10:26,639 --> 00:10:27,840
It's not that you can't.

185
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,360
It's just a bit of a contrast...

186
00:10:29,639 --> 00:10:30,399
And you are...?

187
00:10:30,679 --> 00:10:31,759
I'm a competitor.

188
00:10:31,879 --> 00:10:32,440
Name?

189
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,039
Lin Ran.

190
00:10:35,159 --> 00:10:35,759
Found it.

191
00:10:36,799 --> 00:10:38,240
But your match isn't until later.

192
00:10:38,519 --> 00:10:40,159
I want to warm up first.

193
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,480
But you're way too early.

194
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:43,000
Is that okay?

195
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,279
I suppose so.

196
00:10:44,279 --> 00:10:45,679
But you need to finish before three.

197
00:10:45,679 --> 00:10:47,200
The afternoon matches will start then.

198
00:10:48,159 --> 00:10:48,679
No problem.

199
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,159
Let's go. Don't just stand there.

200
00:10:52,159 --> 00:10:52,799
Go get changed.

201
00:10:54,399 --> 00:10:55,279
Go, hurry up.

202
00:11:08,559 --> 00:11:09,679
Done changing. Come on.

203
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:10,600
Here, give it a try.

204
00:11:11,519 --> 00:11:11,960
No need.

205
00:11:12,279 --> 00:11:13,480
I used to practice a lot in college.

206
00:11:27,399 --> 00:11:28,200
Not bad.

207
00:11:28,559 --> 00:11:29,440
How about

208
00:11:30,279 --> 00:11:30,960
we have a match?

209
00:11:40,559 --> 00:11:41,360
No problem.

210
00:11:42,159 --> 00:11:42,960
Are you ready?

211
00:11:45,759 --> 00:11:46,600
Ready.

212
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,080
Begin!

213
00:12:32,639 --> 00:12:33,159
Here.

214
00:12:33,799 --> 00:12:35,320
You could at least go easy on him.

215
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:37,000
It's your first date.

216
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Don't hurt his ego.

217
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,440
When you play games,

218
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:42,039
I don't see you caring about his ego.

219
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:43,840
It's a competition.

220
00:12:44,559 --> 00:12:47,000
You have to take it seriously, right?

221
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:00,480
You lost.

222
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:04,440
Thanks.

223
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:09,480
But among amateurs,

224
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:10,759
I'm pretty good, right?

225
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Among amateurs, you're average at best.

226
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:25,399
You call this average?

227
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,960
Yeah, very average.

228
00:13:29,399 --> 00:13:30,840
Alright, I'm just kidding.

229
00:13:31,279 --> 00:13:32,080
You're really good.

230
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:35,399
Come on.

231
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,039
The real match starts now.

232
00:13:41,399 --> 00:13:41,799
Wait.

233
00:13:43,279 --> 00:13:44,200
Isn't it already over?

234
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:45,759
That was just a warm up.

235
00:13:46,799 --> 00:13:47,639
Let's go, let's go.

236
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:50,840
Why do I feel like Lin Ran

237
00:13:51,039 --> 00:13:52,399
is starting to like that guy?

238
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:56,799
What about you?

239
00:13:57,639 --> 00:13:58,600
Do you like him?

240
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,679
I wouldn't say I like him,

241
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:02,200
but I don't hate him either.

242
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:03,440
Can you handle this?

243
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:04,399
Yeah.

244
00:14:04,679 --> 00:14:06,200
This is the real match.

245
00:14:06,559 --> 00:14:07,360
Come on.

246
00:14:07,679 --> 00:14:08,279
Speed it up.

247
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:09,080
Go.

248
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:14,679
So have you made a decision?

249
00:14:14,759 --> 00:14:15,559
What decision?

250
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:20,759
To give the time to Lin Ran.
